# Line endings for files the Raspberry Pi (or a Linux cluster) runs or checks byte for byte. With core.autocrlf=true,
# a Windows checkout would otherwise write these with CRLF, and hardware/legobot/deploy.sh ships the working tree.
#
# Shell scripts: bash can't parse CRLF (robot/run_safe.sh failed on the Pi with $'\r': command not found).
*.sh text eol=lf
# Policy bundles: manifest.json's files_sha256 (checked by the robot before it runs a policy) covers the exact
# bytes export_policy.py wrote, so git must neither convert them on checkout nor normalize them on commit.
results/legobot/policies/** -text
*.npz binary
